message: "If you reference Guardian F401, please cite the archived release."
title: "Guardian F401: Deterministic Embedded Decision Assurance for Machine Health, Cybersecurity, and Supervisory Control"
version: "0.14.0"
date-released: "2026-08-16"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Antonio José"
    family-names: "Socorro Marín"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9089-9222"
repository-code: "https://github.com/socorromipunto-eng/guardian-f401"
url: "https://github.com/socorromipunto-eng/guardian-f401"
abstract: >-
  Guardian F401 is an experimental STM32F401CDU6 embedded research platform
  combining deterministic signal acquisition, DSP and spectral analysis,
  machine-health state evaluation, supervisory control, authenticated command
  handling, robustness testing, a portable signed-firmware lifecycle, and a
  bounded software-assurance slice with deterministic canonicalization and
  closed payload contracts. Software validation is documented; physical board
  qualification and safety certification are not claimed.
keywords:
  - "embedded systems"
  - "STM32F401"
  - "cybersecurity"
  - "firmware integrity"
  - "deterministic control"
  - "decision assurance"
  - "bounded assurance"
  - "canonicalization"
  - "digital signal processing"
  - "machine condition monitoring"
